{"uid":"sn2.7","title":"With Pañcālacaṇḍa","reference":"Saṁyutta Nikāya 2.7","blocks":[{"kind":"prose","lines":["At Sāvatthī."]},{"kind":"prose","lines":["Standing to one side, the godling Pañcālacaṇḍa spoke this verse in the Buddha’s presence:"]},{"kind":"verse","lines":["“The opening amid confinement","was discovered by the Buddha of vast intelligence,","who awakened to absorption,","the sage, the solitary boss bull.”","“Even amid confinement they understand,”"]},{"kind":"prose","lines":["said the Buddha to Pañcālacaṇḍa,"]},{"kind":"verse","lines":["“the principle for attaining extinguishment.","Those who have acquired mindfulness","are perfectly serene in samādhi.”"]}]}
